.TH AWAPP 1 "August 2026" "awapp 1.0.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
awapp \- dependency-free terminal weather visualizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B awapp
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B awapp
polls a weather source and renders the current condition as a
full-screen ANSI animation: sun/moon arcs, real star positions (from your
location and the local sidereal time), seasonal leaves/snow, rain, clouds
and more. It needs no API key by default (Open-Meteo + IP geolocation);
an OpenWeatherMap key is optional for a named-city source.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-apikey " KEY"
OpenWeatherMap API key (or config file / OPENWEATHERMAP_API_KEY env).
.TP
.BR \-\-city " CITY"
City to fetch, e.g. "Fortaleza,BR"; no API key needed.
.TP
.BR \-\-use\-ip
Use IP-location weather (ipinfo + Open-Meteo) instead of an API key.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-ip\-prompt
Skip the interactive IP-location prompt (for scripted/systemd use).
.TP
.BR \-\-interval " DURATION"
How often to poll the weather API (default 5m).
.TP
.BR \-\-fps " N"
Animation frame rate (default 15).
.TP
.BR \-f
Start with Fahrenheit display.
.TP
.BR \-\-color
Enable 256-color output (default: monochrome).
.TP
.BR \-\-stars " MODE"
Star field: light, full, off.
.TP
.BR \-\-light\-key " KEY"
lightpollutionmap.info key for exact light-pollution readings.
.TP
.BR \-\-moon " MODE"
Moon visibility: auto, on, off.
.TP
.BR \-\-phase " 0..1"
Override the moon phase (default: compute from date).
.TP
.BR \-\-eclipse
Start a simulated lunar eclipse.
.TP
.BR \-\-eclipse\-duration " DURATION"
Length of a simulated lunar eclipse.
.TP
.BR \-\-solar\-eclipse
Start a simulated solar eclipse.
.TP
.BR \-\-solar\-eclipse\-duration " DURATION"
Length of a simulated solar eclipse.
.TP
.BR \-\-size " PCT"
Sun/Moon diameter as % of terminal width (4..60, default 15).
.TP
.BR \-\-season " SEASON"
Leaf season: auto, spring, summer, fall, winter.
.TP
.BR \-\-leaves
Enable the seasonal leaf/snow layer (default on).
.TP
.BR \-\-save\-config
On quit, write the last-used color/units/stars toggles back to the
config file.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-config
Print the resolved configuration (and each value's source) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " PATH"
Path to a config.json (default: ~/.config/awapp/config.json).
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B s
Show/hide the status panel.
.TP
.B u
Toggle C / F.
.TP
.B c
Toggle color.
.TP
.B t
Cycle stars: light-pollution sim, hidden, full.
.TP
.B o
Toggle clouds.
.TP
.B l
Toggle the seasonal leaf/snow layer.
.TP
.B m
Cycle moon: auto, on, off.
.TP
.B e / x
Toggle a simulated lunar / solar eclipse.
.TP
.BR + / \-
Resize the Sun/Moon.
.TP
.BR 1 \- 5
Offline: pick clear / clouds / rain / snow / thunderstorm manually.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH CONFIG
Configuration precedence: command-line flags > environment variables >
config file (~/.config/awapp/config.json) > defaults. Run
.B awapp \-\-list\-config
to see which source each setting came from. The config file may hold a
plaintext API key, so keep it readable only by you (chmod 600).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENWEATHERMAP_API_KEY / OPENWEATHER_API_KEY
API key fallback.
.TP
.B OPENWEATHERMAP_CITY / OPENWEATHER_CITY
City fallback.
.TP
.B LIGHT_POLLUTION_MAP_API_KEY
Light-pollution key fallback.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error (e.g. no usable weather source).
.SH AUTHOR
rodlessa (https://github.com/rodlessa/awapp)
